[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Atomic Operations
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-37-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Basic Atomic Read and Write

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic read
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically read the value of an atomic
variable.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to read and write integer variables shared between threads
and ISRs without the need for a mutex or spinlock.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic write
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically set the value of an atomic
variable and return its previous value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic clear
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically set an atomic variable to zero
and return its previous value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[[/SECTION]]

