[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Atomic Bit Manipulation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic set bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically set a specified bit in an
atomic variable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic clear bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically clear a specified bit in an
atomic variable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic test bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically test whether a specified bit
in an atomic variable is set.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic test and set bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically test whether a specified bit
in an atomic variable is set and then set that bit, returning the previous bit value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic test and clear bit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically test whether a specified bit
in an atomic variable is set and then clear that bit, returning the previous bit value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Compare and Swap

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic compare and swap
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to atomically compare the value of an atomic
variable with an expected value and, if equal, replace it with a new value, returning
an indication of whether the swap occurred.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a compare-and-swap primitive to implement lock-free data
structures and synchronization algorithms.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-29

[[/SECTION]]
